1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,585
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,900
Episode 6.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,471
The Map with a Missing Key.

4
00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:10,497
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,497 --> 00:00:14,232
What did the star mean on this particular map?

6
00:00:14,232 --> 00:00:15,823
Ready?

7
00:00:15,823 --> 00:00:18,025
Let us find out.

8
00:00:18,025 --> 00:00:21,747
Maya finds a map for the school treasure hunt.

9
00:00:21,747 --> 00:00:24,801
A star sits beside a square.

10
00:00:24,801 --> 00:00:27,798
A blue line crosses the page.

11
00:00:27,798 --> 00:00:31,335
Three green circles stand near the bottom.

12
00:00:31,335 --> 00:00:34,744
The star must be treasure, says Leo.

13
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:36,988
Pip disagrees.

14
00:00:36,988 --> 00:00:40,340
It could be a spaceship parking area.

15
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:43,792
They walk to the place marked with a star.

16
00:00:43,792 --> 00:00:46,349
It is the school office.

17
00:00:46,349 --> 00:00:51,477
There is no treasure, and the secretary has not seen any spaceships.

18
00:00:51,477 --> 00:00:54,034
Do you have the map key?

19
00:00:54,034 --> 00:00:56,051
she asks.

20
00:00:56,051 --> 00:00:59,318
We do not need a key, says Leo.

21
00:00:59,318 --> 00:01:01,477
Nothing is locked.

22
00:01:01,477 --> 00:01:05,355
A map key explains the symbols, she tells him.

23
00:01:05,355 --> 00:01:08,096
It is also called a legend.

24
00:01:08,096 --> 00:01:11,732
Maya unfolds the bottom of the paper.

25
00:01:11,732 --> 00:01:13,650
There it is.

26
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:16,803
The star means information desk.

27
00:01:16,803 --> 00:01:19,303
The square means building.

28
00:01:19,303 --> 00:01:24,204
The blue line is a stream, and the green circles are large trees.

29
00:01:24,204 --> 00:01:27,258
Now the first clue makes sense.

30
00:01:27,258 --> 00:01:30,312
Start at the information desk.

31
00:01:30,312 --> 00:01:32,798
Turn right at the stream.

32
00:01:32,798 --> 00:01:35,610
Look beside the three trees.

33
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:39,573
They follow the instructions and find a small box.

34
00:01:39,573 --> 00:01:42,301
Inside is the next clue.

35
00:01:42,301 --> 00:01:44,417
Pip looks proud.

36
00:01:44,417 --> 00:01:47,727
My navigation system is excellent.

37
00:01:47,727 --> 00:01:52,784
You thought the office was a spaceship parking area, Leo reminds him.

38
00:01:52,784 --> 00:01:56,917
That possibility has now been removed, says Pip.

39
00:01:56,917 --> 00:02:01,832
Maya puts the map away carefully, with the key still visible.

40
00:02:01,832 --> 00:02:05,639
This time, they know what their information means.

41
00:02:05,639 --> 00:02:08,792
Now, a little more to discover.

42
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:13,536
Maps use symbols to show places without drawing every detail.

43
00:02:13,536 --> 00:02:16,718
A map key explains those symbols.

44
00:02:16,718 --> 00:02:20,525
A direction arrow can help you orient the map.

45
00:02:20,525 --> 00:02:27,613
Symbols are useful only when readers know what they mean; a star does not always mean the same thing on every map.

46
00:02:27,613 --> 00:02:30,781
Let us hear the main idea again.

47
00:02:30,781 --> 00:02:35,639
The children guessed what the map's symbols meant and went to the wrong place.

48
00:02:35,639 --> 00:02:40,951
After reading the key, they understood the star, stream, and trees.

49
00:02:40,951 --> 00:02:45,767
Clear meanings turned a confusing picture into useful directions.

50
00:02:45,767 --> 00:02:48,906
Here are three useful expressions.

51
00:02:48,906 --> 00:02:52,088
You can listen, or say them with me.

52
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:54,161
Excuse me.

53
00:02:54,161 --> 00:02:56,392
Where is the office?

54
00:02:56,392 --> 00:02:58,465
Excuse me.

55
00:02:58,465 --> 00:03:00,696
Where is the office?

56
00:03:00,696 --> 00:03:03,181
Turn right at the stream.

57
00:03:03,181 --> 00:03:05,667
Turn right at the stream.

58
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:08,338
It is next to the trees.

59
00:03:08,338 --> 00:03:11,008
It is next to the trees.

60
00:03:11,008 --> 00:03:14,005
Remember our listening question?

61
00:03:14,005 --> 00:03:17,741
What did the star mean on this particular map?

62
00:03:17,741 --> 00:03:20,028
Here is the answer.

63
00:03:20,028 --> 00:03:23,082
It meant the information desk.

64
00:03:23,082 --> 00:03:26,079
The map key explained its meaning.

65
00:03:26,079 --> 00:03:30,042
And here is a question just for your imagination.

66
00:03:30,042 --> 00:03:34,048
What symbol would you invent for a quiet reading spot?

67
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:36,463
How would you explain it?

68
00:03:36,463 --> 00:03:39,772
There is more than one possible answer.

69
00:03:39,772 --> 00:03:43,068
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
